 // However, in most cases it is more convenient to use a more specific function like `expectEqual`. // This gives you much clearer and more helpful error messages when a test fails. try  std.testing.expectEqual( 42 , addOne( 41 ));
```
}
test  addOne {
// A test name can also be written using an identifier. // This is a doctest, and serves as documentation for `addOne`. try  std.testing.expectEqual( 42 , addOne( 41 ));
